{"base_rate":0.1761827079934747,"brier":0.12455122349102772,"bss":0.14186856068940235,"bss_hi":0.2610811253223833,"bss_lo":-0.0066094576348035,"chart":{"base":[214.3,207.4],"fp":[237.9,125.7],"lead":"62,229.7 272,205.8 482,170.6 692,117.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.14 — higher than 21% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +28pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 26% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 2%; promised 74% → rained 52%"},"rel":"62,455.9 104,431.7 234.8,376 527.1,243.2"},"country":"AZ","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07088091353996735,"ess":465.51997867802135,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ganja</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ganja rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (87%), believe about\n<b>48%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 613 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 6.1 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.14, ranked 170 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(120&ndash;191) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>214</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>13%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>29%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>87%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ganja</b> <span class=\"muted\">Azerbaijan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;18% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 18% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better. The difference is within the margin of error.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.14</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>120&ndash;191\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>613 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ganja &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ganja\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.49625,350.15 92.9512676056338,320.4788732394366 126.7248275862069,275.3103448275862 181.61451612903224,211.74193548387098 269.37225806451613,117.80645161290323 366.30181818181813,34.545454545454504 366.30181818181813,95.21212121212125 269.37225806451613,205.8709677419355 181.61451612903224,293.93548387096774 126.7248275862069,344.3448275862069 92.9512676056338,366.61971830985914 71.49625,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"317.8694942903752\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"317.8694942903752\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,373.49532710280374 71.49625,368.35 92.9512676056338,335.85915492957747 126.7248275862069,338.0689655172414 181.61451612903224,276.3225806451613 269.37225806451613,182.38709677419357 366.30181818181813,205.5151515151515\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 214 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"373.49532710280374\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.49625\" cy=\"368.35\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 13% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"92.9512676056338\" cy=\"335.85915492957747\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 58 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"126.7248275862069\" cy=\"338.0689655172414\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 29% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"181.61451612903224\" cy=\"276.3225806451613\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 60%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 62 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"269.37225806451613\" cy=\"182.38709677419357\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 87%&amp;#10;It rained 48% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"366.30181818181813\" cy=\"205.5151515151515\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(18%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Ganja the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>summer</b> (0.31) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>163</td><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'>-0.146</td><td class='num'>9.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>130</td><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'>0.057</td><td class='num'>8.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>157</td><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'>0.271</td><td class='num'>6.8%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>163</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>0.306</td><td class='num'>5.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":40.68157,"lon":46.36134,"n":613,"n_cities":216,"name":"Ganja","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":214,"obs":0.02336448598130841,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.038125,"n":80,"obs":0.0375,"sig":false},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.09873239436619716,"n":71,"obs":0.1267605633802817,"sig":false},{"hi":0.28,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.19413793103448276,"n":58,"obs":0.1206896551724138,"sig":false},{"hi":0.48,"lo":0.28,"mean":0.3491935483870967,"n":62,"obs":0.2903225806451613,"sig":false},{"hi":0.75,"lo":0.48,"mean":0.5970967741935483,"n":62,"obs":0.5483870967741935,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.75,"mean":0.8709090909090909,"n":66,"obs":0.48484848484848486,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":6.1,"provisional":false,"rank":170,"rank_hi":191.02499999999998,"rank_lo":120.0,"reliability":0.01742956915482176,"resolution":0.03682444026154601,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"ganja","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Baku"}